---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import { founders, foundingFaculty } from '../data/people.js';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Some do. Some teach. A few do both. Those are the people we build programs around."
>

  <!-- ============ WHY ============ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell shell--narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why we exist</p>
      <h1 class="display h2">Some do. Some teach. <span class="accent">A few do both.</span></h1>
      <div class="body" style="margin-top:26px; font-size:1.06rem;">
        <p>Those are the people we look for, and the only people we build a program around.</p>

        <p>Executive education keeps the two apart. The institution's name goes on the
        certificate, but the person teaching is rarely the person who built the thing being
        taught. Programs are delivered by platforms, at scale, by facilitators working from
        someone else's material.</p>

        <p>Gregory La Blanc has spent his career in academia and never stayed inside it. He
        brings people from industry into his classrooms, and he sends his fellow faculty out
        to talk to practitioners. What he kept finding is that the people fluent in both
        worlds tell the best stories, draw the sharpest lessons, and reach the people who
        actually need them. Nobody had built those people a vehicle worth their time.</p>

        <p>So he called Polina Nazarova, someone he had been working with for a couple of
        years through his teaching in Spain. She runs corporate partnerships at
        Harbour.Space in Barcelona, a university built on the same premise: the people
        teaching should be the people still doing the work.</p>

        <p>The Silicon Valley Faculty Network came out of that. Find the person who did the
        work and can also teach it. Build the program around them rather than fitting them
        into a curriculum. Keep the cohort small enough that access is real. Put their name
        on it rather than an institution's.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- ============ PHILOSOPHY ============ -->
  <section>
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
      <h2 class="display h3" style="margin-bottom:28px;">Four decisions we do not trade away.</h2>
      <div class="rows" data-rise-group>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Faculty first, syllabus second</h3>
          <p>Every program starts with a person, not a topic. We find someone who defined a
          field, then design the program around what they know and how they teach. It is why
          the programs look different from each other, and why we cannot simply add a course
          because there is demand for one.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Around thirty seats, on purpose</h3>
          <p>Small is the product, not a limitation. Comparable programs delivered through
          platforms run cohorts of several hundred. At thirty, the session stays a discussion,
          the faculty member knows who you are, and your question gets answered rather than
          logged.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Useful on Monday</h3>
          <p>You arrive with a real problem from your own organization and work on it
          throughout. You leave with a plan you can act on, and a certificate as a side
          effect rather than the reason you came.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>A house of programs, not a brand on a course</h3>
          <p>Each program is convened with a different lead practitioner who teaches it and
          brings their own network to it. We are the institute that makes that possible: the
          structure, the cohort, the operations. The expertise belongs to the person whose
          name is on the program.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- ============ FOUNDING TEAM ============ -->
  <section>
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Founding team</p>
      <h2 class="display h3" style="margin-bottom:26px;">Who started it.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2" data-rise-group>
        {founders.map((p) => (
          <article class="card person">
            <Portrait src={p.photo} name={p.name} size="lg" />
            <p class="label">{p.role}</p>
            <h3 class="display h4">{p.name}</h3>
            <p>{p.bio ?? <span class="todo">bio, 60 to 80 words</span>}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- ============ FOUNDING FACULTY ============ -->
  <section>
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Founding faculty</p>
      <h2 class="display h3" style="margin-bottom:10px;">The people who agreed first.</h2>
      <p class="body" style="margin-bottom:26px;">
        They convene the programs, teach them, and shape what we build next.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid--3" data-rise-group>
        {foundingFaculty.map((p) => (
          <article class="card person">
            <Portrait src={p.photo} name={p.name} size="lg" />
            <p class="label">{p.role}</p>
            <h3 class="display h4">{p.name}</h3>
            <p>{p.bio ?? <span class="todo">bio, 60 to 80 words</span>}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="body" style="margin-top:26px;">
        This list grows slowly, and deliberately. A program goes on sale only once the
        person teaching it has agreed to teach it, which means the pipeline moves at the
        speed of people rather than the speed of demand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ CLOSING ============ -->
  <section class="closing">
    <div class="shell center">
      <h2 class="display h3" style="color:var(--bone)">Want to teach with us?</h2>
      <p style="color:rgba(245,243,238,.78); margin:16px auto 26px; max-width:48ch;">
        We are always looking for the person who built the thing, not the person who wrote
        about it afterwards.
      </p>
      <div class="btnrow" style="justify-content:center;">
        <a href="/teach" class="btn btn--solid">Teach with us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(48px, 7vw, 84px); }
  .hero .body p { margin-bottom: 18px; }

  .person h3 { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
  .person .label { margin: 14px 0 0; }
  .person p:last-child { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .92rem; margin: 0; }

  .closing { background: var(--ink); }
</style>
